{
    "name": "shade-light",
    "label": "Shade (light)",
    "selector": "[data-theme='shade-light']",
    "entries": [
        {
            "raw": "    /* Shade, the light half: a book read in the shade, not in the sun. Solarized-derived, medium contrast, accents as plates. */"
        },
        {
            "token": "background",
            "value": "hsl(44, 87%, 94%)"
        },
        {
            "token": "foreground",
            "value": "hsl(194, 14%, 36%)",
            "why": "`scope-102` (Kenny, 2026-09-16, shade-light-muted \"Gewone tekst ook donkerder\"): the body ink was 40% lightness, one step DARKER than the muted ink `scope-101` had pushed to 39%, so shade-light's quiet text read stronger than its running text on all three grounds (body 4.52 / muted 4.71 on --muted, 4.99 / 5.21 on --background, 5.17 / 5.39 on --card). Darkening the body ink to 36% puts the order back without moving the muted ink: 5.30 / 4.71, 5.86 / 5.21, 6.07 / 5.39 — the muted ink is 0.59, 0.65 and 0.68 quieter, past the 0.5 asked for, and both inks clear 4.5:1 on every ground. Solarized's own base01 `#586e75` is the 40% value; 36% is that ink deepened, the same hue and saturation, and still far from black (anatomy.md's \"no black\" line now reads 36%). --card-foreground, --popover-foreground, --surface-hero-fg and --surface-hero-card-foreground carry the same ink and move with it: one ink, one value."
        },
