        {
            "token": "muted-foreground",
            "value": "hsl(194, 14%, 39%)",
            "why": "Phase 7, `shade-light-muted`, Kenny 2026-09-12: this was identical to --foreground, the only theme of twenty-two where the two matched, so nothing in shade-light was actually muted, and it was lightened to 46%. Darkened to 39% at `scope-101` (Kenny, 2026-09-16, shade-light-contrast \"Donkerder maken\"): at 46% the three pairs measured 3.61 on muted, 3.99 on background and 4.13 on card, and they now measure 4.71, 5.21 and 5.39. That cleared the floor but inverted the order — the body ink, still at 40%, reached only 4.52 on --muted, so the quiet text read STRONGER than the running text on all three grounds. `scope-102` (Kenny, 2026-09-16, shade-light-muted \"Gewone tekst ook donkerder\") answered that by darkening the body ink instead of lightening this one: --foreground went to 36% and this token stayed at 39%, so the order is muted BEHIND body again — 4.71 against 5.30 on --muted, 5.21 against 5.86 on --background, 5.39 against 6.07 on --card, 0.59 to 0.68 of separation with both inks over 4.5:1. No colour lighter than the old 40% body ink could have done it (the best that existed was 0.02:1 quieter, hsl(194, 24%, 39%) at 4.50/4.97/5.15); moving the body ink is what made the order reachable."
        },
